MOS v0.1 Stabilization & Cross-Spec Validation
1. Stabilization objective

We currently have these major specifications:

MOS Core Specification v0.1
MOS Storage Specification v0.1
MOS API Specification v0.1
MOS Worker Specification v0.1
MOS Attention & Reasoning Gateway
MOS Network Specification v0.1
RFC-0001 → RFC-0014

The stabilization process must answer five questions:

Do all specifications use the same concepts?
Do they use the same terminology?
Can every object be traced from creation → storage → processing → retrieval → network propagation?
Are ownership, provenance, versioning and lifecycle consistent everywhere?
Can we actually implement v0.1 without inventing missing concepts?

The last question is particularly important.

A specification is not stable merely because it sounds complete. It is stable when an engineer can implement it without repeatedly asking:

"What does the specification mean here?"

