3. The most important distinction: source vs projection

One of the biggest things we should freeze now is this:

Authoritative objects

These represent actual MOS knowledge/state.

Event
Entity
Fact
Relationship
Goal
Task
Procedure
Skill
Observation
Plan
Provenance
Derived objects

These can be reconstructed.

Embedding
Vector index
Search index
Graph projection
Summary
Cache
Ranking
Materialized retrieval context
Statistics

This distinction needs to exist across all specifications.

Otherwise we eventually get into a situation where:

PostgreSQL says X
Vector DB says Y
Graph says Z
Cache says W

and nobody knows which one is authoritative.

The rule should be:

Derived cognitive representations never become the authoritative source of truth unless explicitly promoted by a MOS operation.

